        },
        "quote": "If a contractor has not paid for permits within 30 days from the date of notice to pay permit fees, it shall be deemed the contractor is working without a permit and all work in progress shall stop. Any contractor who fails to pay permit fees within 30 days of notice to pay shall be required to pay for permits in advance for six months thereafter. (Code 1981 § 10-40.5. Code 1995 § 26-56.)",
